/* BAIO Exam Scorer — II PUC Biology pass-first material, by Narendra Sir. m/bp = KSEAB blueprint, Model Question Paper I (2024-25): marks out of 105 and [1M,2M,3M,5M] questions */
window.EXAM_SCORER = [{"ch":1,"t":"Sexual Reproduction in Flowering Plants","m":"11","plan":"Highest-scoring chapter. Learn the 4 diagrams first (anther T.S., embryo sac, anatropous ovule, dicot embryo) — diagrams alone can fetch 8–10 marks.","kn":"ಹೂವಿನಲ್ಲಿ ಗಂಡು ಭಾಗ (ಪರಾಗಕೋಶ) ಪರಾಗಕಣಗಳನ್ನು, ಹೆಣ್ಣು ಭಾಗ (ಅಂಡಕ) ಭ್ರೂಣಕೋಶವನ್ನು ಮಾಡುತ್ತದೆ. ಪರಾಗಸ್ಪರ್ಶದ ನಂತರ ದ್ವಿನಿಷೇಚನ ಆಗಿ ಬೀಜ ಮತ್ತು ಹಣ್ಣು ರೂಪುಗೊಳ್ಳುತ್ತವೆ.","hi":"फूल का नर भाग (परागकोश) परागकण बनाता है और मादा भाग (बीजांड) भ्रूणकोश बनाता है। परागण के बाद द्विनिषेचन होता है और बीज व फल बनते हैं।","qs":[{"mk":5,"q":"Describe the structure of a microsporangium (T.S. of anther) and microsporogenesis.","a":["Anther is bilobed, dithecous and tetrasporangiate (4 microsporangia).","Wall layers from outside: epidermis, endothecium, 2–3 middle layers, tapetum (innermost).","Tapetum nourishes the developing pollen grains.","Centre has sporogenous tissue; each cell can act as a microspore mother cell (pollen mother cell, 2n).","Microsporogenesis: PMC undergoes meiosis → microspore tetrad (4 cells, n).","Microspores separate and develop into pollen grains.","Draw the labelled T.S. of anther."],"kn":"ಪರಾಗಕೋಶದ 4 ಗೋಡೆ ಪದರಗಳು + ಮಿಯೋಸಿಸ್‌ನಿಂದ 4 ಪರಾಗಕಣಗಳು.","hi":"परागकोश की 4 दीवार परतें + अर्धसूत्रण से 4 परागकण।"},{"mk":5,"q":"Explain the development of the female gametophyte (embryo sac).","a":["Megaspore mother cell (2n) in the nucellus undergoes meiosis → 4 megaspores (n).","3 megaspores degenerate; 1 functional megaspore remains (monosporic development).","Its nucleus divides by mitosis 3 times (free nuclear) → 8 nuclei.","Cell walls form → 7-celled, 8-nucleate embryo sac.","Micropylar end: egg apparatus = 1 egg + 2 synergids (with filiform apparatus).","Chalazal end: 3 antipodal cells.","Centre: 1 large central cell with 2 polar nuclei."],"kn":"1 ಕ್ರಿಯಾಶೀಲ ಮೆಗಾಸ್ಪೋರ್ → 3 ಬಾರಿ ಮೈಟೋಸಿಸ್ → 8 ಕೋಶಕೇಂದ್ರ, 7 ಕೋಶಗಳು.","hi":"1 क्रियाशील गुरुबीजाणु → 3 बार समसूत्रण → 8 केंद्रक, 7 कोशिकाएँ।"},{"mk":5,"q":"What is double fertilisation? Explain.","a":["Pollen tube enters the ovule through the micropyle and the embryo sac through a synergid.","It releases 2 male gametes.","Syngamy: one male gamete + egg → zygote (2n) → embryo.","Triple fusion: second male gamete + 2 polar nuclei → primary endosperm nucleus (3n) → endosperm.","Since two fusions occur in one embryo sac, it is called double fertilisation.","It is unique to flowering plants."],"kn":"ಎರಡು ಸಮ್ಮಿಲನ: ಸಿಂಗ್ಯಾಮಿ (ಯುಗ್ಮಜ 2n) + ತ್ರಿಸಮ್ಮಿಲನ (ಭ್ರೂಣಪೋಷಕ 3n).","hi":"दो संलयन: युग्मक संलयन (युग्मनज 2n) + त्रिसंलयन (भ्रूणपोष 3n)।"},{"mk":3,"q":"Describe the structure of a pollen grain.","a":["Two-layered wall: outer exine and inner intine.","Exine is made of sporopollenin — very hard, resists high temperature, acids and alkalis.","Exine has germ pores where sporopollenin is absent; pollen tube comes out through them.","Intine is thin, made of cellulose and pectin.","Mature pollen has 2 cells: a large vegetative cell and a small generative cell."],"kn":"ಹೊರಗೋಡೆ ಎಕ್ಸೈನ್ (ಸ್ಪೋರೊಪೊಲೆನಿನ್), ಒಳಗೋಡೆ ಇಂಟೈನ್; ಸಸ್ಯಕೋಶ + ಜನನಕೋಶ.","hi":"बाहरी भित्ति एक्साइन (स्पोरोपोलेनिन), भीतरी इन्टाइन; कायिक + जनन कोशिका।"},{"mk":3,"q":"What are outbreeding devices? Give three.","a":["Devices that prevent self-pollination and encourage cross-pollination.","Pollen release and stigma receptivity at different times (dichogamy).","Anther and stigma placed at different positions.","Self-incompatibility — self pollen cannot fertilise the ovule.","Unisexual flowers / dioecy (e.g. papaya)."],"kn":"ಸ್ವಪರಾಗಸ್ಪರ್ಶ ತಡೆಯುವ ವಿಧಾನಗಳು.","hi":"स्वपरागण रोकने के उपाय।"},{"mk":3,"q":"Define apomixis and polyembryony with examples.","a":["Apomixis: formation of seeds without fertilisation (asexual reproduction that mimics sexual reproduction).","Seen in some Asteraceae and grasses.","Polyembryony: more than one embryo in a seed.","Seen in Citrus and Mango (nucellar cells form extra embryos)."],"kn":"ಅಪೊಮಿಕ್ಸಿಸ್ = ನಿಷೇಚನವಿಲ್ಲದೆ ಬೀಜ; ಬಹುಭ್ರೂಣತೆ = ಒಂದು ಬೀಜದಲ್ಲಿ ಅನೇಕ ಭ್ರೂಣ.","hi":"असंगजनन = बिना निषेचन बीज; बहुभ्रूणता = एक बीज में कई भ्रूण।"},{"mk":2,"q":"What is emasculation? Why is bagging done?","a":["Emasculation: removing anthers from a bisexual flower bud before they dehisce.","Bagging: covering the emasculated flower with a butter-paper bag to prevent contamination by unwanted pollen."],"kn":"ಪರಾಗಕೋಶ ತೆಗೆಯುವುದು; ಬೇರೆ ಪರಾಗ ಬೀಳದಂತೆ ಚೀಲ ಮುಚ್ಚುವುದು.","hi":"परागकोश हटाना; अनचाहा पराग रोकने के लिए थैली चढ़ाना।"},{"mk":2,"q":"What is parthenocarpy? Give an example.","a":["Development of fruit without fertilisation (seedless fruit).","Example: banana. Can be induced by growth hormones."],"kn":"ನಿಷೇಚನವಿಲ್ಲದೆ ಹಣ್ಣು — ಉದಾ: ಬಾಳೆ.","hi":"बिना निषेचन फल — उदा: केला।"}],"dia":[{"n":"T.S. of anther (microsporangium)","l":["Epidermis","Endothecium","Middle layers","Tapetum","Sporogenous tissue / microspore tetrad","Connective"]},{"n":"Mature embryo sac","l":["Egg","Synergids","Filiform apparatus","Central cell with polar nuclei","Antipodals","Micropylar end","Chalazal end"]},{"n":"Anatropous ovule","l":["Funicle","Hilum","Micropyle","Integuments","Nucellus","Embryo sac","Chalaza"]},{"n":"Dicot embryo","l":["Plumule","Cotyledons","Epicotyl","Hypocotyl","Radicle","Root cap"]}],"facts":["Pollen wall exine is made of sporopollenin.","Tapetum is the innermost, nourishing wall layer of the anther.","Embryo sac is 7-celled and 8-nucleate.","Endosperm is triploid (3n).","Filiform apparatus guides the pollen tube.","Water-pollinated plant: Vallisneria / Zostera.","Autogamy, geitonogamy and xenogamy are the 3 types of pollination.","Seeds without fertilisation = apomixis."],"trick":["Anther wall, outside → in: \"Every Elephant Must Trumpet\" = Epidermis, Endothecium, Middle layers, Tapetum.","Embryo sac \"3 + 2 + 3\": 3 at micropyle (egg apparatus), 2 polar nuclei in the middle, 3 antipodals at chalaza."],"bp":[1,1,1,1]},{"ch":2,"t":"Human Reproduction","m":"10","plan":"Big chapter. Secure the menstrual cycle, oogenesis/spermatogenesis flow and the testis / ovary diagrams. Write answers as flow-charts.","kn":"ಗಂಡು ಮತ್ತು ಹೆಣ್ಣು ಸಂತಾನೋತ್ಪತ್ತಿ ಅಂಗಗಳು, ವೀರ್ಯ ಮತ್ತು ಅಂಡಾಣು ರಚನೆ, ಋತುಚಕ್ರ, ನಿಷೇಚನ, ಗರ್ಭ ಮತ್ತು ಹೆರಿಗೆ — ಇದು ಈ ಅಧ್ಯಾಯದ ಕಥೆ.","hi":"पुरुष और स्त्री जनन अंग, शुक्राणु और अंडाणु बनना, मासिक चक्र, निषेचन, गर्भ और प्रसव — यही इस अध्याय की कहानी है।","qs":[{"mk":5,"q":"Explain the menstrual cycle with its phases and hormones.","a":["Cycle of about 28 days; first menstruation is menarche, stopping at ~50 years is menopause.","Menstrual phase (days 1–5): endometrium breaks down and bleeding occurs, because the egg was not fertilised.","Follicular / proliferative phase (days 6–13): FSH and LH rise; follicle grows and secretes oestrogen; endometrium regenerates.","Ovulation (about day 14): LH surge causes the Graafian follicle to rupture and release the ovum.","Luteal / secretory phase (days 15–28): corpus luteum forms and secretes progesterone, which maintains the endometrium.","If no fertilisation, corpus luteum degenerates → progesterone falls → next menstruation."],"kn":"ಋತುಸ್ರಾವ → ಕೋಶಕ ಹಂತ → ಅಂಡೋತ್ಸರ್ಗ (LH) → ಲ್ಯೂಟಿಯಲ್ ಹಂತ (ಪ್ರೊಜೆಸ್ಟೆರಾನ್).","hi":"मासिक स्राव → पुटक प्रावस्था → अंडोत्सर्ग (LH) → पीत प्रावस्था (प्रोजेस्टेरोन)।"},{"mk":5,"q":"Describe oogenesis.","a":["Begins in the foetal ovary: oogonia (2n) form by mitosis.","Oogonia enter meiosis-I and stop at prophase-I → primary oocytes.","Primary oocyte + granulosa cells = primary follicle → secondary follicle → tertiary follicle (antrum).","At puberty, primary oocyte completes meiosis-I → secondary oocyte (n) + first polar body.","Tertiary follicle becomes the Graafian follicle; secondary oocyte is released at ovulation.","Meiosis-II completes only when a sperm enters → ovum + second polar body."],"kn":"ಊಗೋನಿಯಾ → ಪ್ರಾಥಮಿಕ ಊಸೈಟ್ → ದ್ವಿತೀಯ ಊಸೈಟ್ → ಅಂಡಾಣು (ಧ್ರುವಕಾಯಗಳೊಂದಿಗೆ).","hi":"अंडजननी → प्राथमिक अंडक → द्वितीयक अंडक → अंडाणु (ध्रुवीय पिंडों के साथ)।"},{"mk":5,"q":"Explain spermatogenesis and its hormonal control.","a":["Occurs in seminiferous tubules from puberty.","Spermatogonia (2n) multiply by mitosis → primary spermatocytes (2n).","Primary spermatocyte → meiosis-I → 2 secondary spermatocytes (n).","Meiosis-II → 4 spermatids (n) → spermiogenesis → spermatozoa.","GnRH from hypothalamus → pituitary releases LH and FSH.","LH acts on Leydig cells → androgens (testosterone); FSH acts on Sertoli cells → helps spermiogenesis."],"kn":"ಸ್ಪರ್ಮಟೋಗೋನಿಯಾ → ಸ್ಪರ್ಮಟೋಸೈಟ್ → ಸ್ಪರ್ಮಟಿಡ್ → ವೀರ್ಯಾಣು; GnRH, LH, FSH.","hi":"शुक्राणुजन → शुक्राणुकोशिका → शुक्राणुप्रसू → शुक्राणु; GnRH, LH, FSH।"},{"mk":3,"q":"Explain the process of fertilisation.","a":["Fertilisation takes place in the ampullary region of the fallopian tube.","Sperm contacts the zona pellucida; acrosome enzymes help it enter.","Entry of one sperm blocks other sperms.","Secondary oocyte completes meiosis-II → ovum + second polar body.","Haploid nuclei of sperm and ovum fuse → diploid zygote."],"kn":"ಅಂಡನಾಳದ ಆಂಪುಲ್ಲಾದಲ್ಲಿ ವೀರ್ಯ + ಅಂಡಾಣು → ಯುಗ್ಮಜ.","hi":"अंडवाहिनी के तुंबिका भाग में शुक्राणु + अंडाणु → युग्मनज।"},{"mk":3,"q":"What is the placenta? Write its functions.","a":["Structural and functional unit between the embryo (chorionic villi) and the mother's uterine wall.","Supplies oxygen and nutrients to the embryo.","Removes carbon dioxide and wastes.","Acts as an endocrine gland: secretes hCG, hPL, oestrogens and progesterone."],"kn":"ತಾಯಿ–ಭ್ರೂಣ ಸಂಪರ್ಕ; ಆಹಾರ, ಆಮ್ಲಜನಕ ಸರಬರಾಜು; ಹಾರ್ಮೋನ್ ಸ್ರವಿಸುತ್ತದೆ.","hi":"माँ–भ्रूण संबंध; भोजन, ऑक्सीजन देता है; हार्मोन बनाता है।"},{"mk":3,"q":"Name the male accessory glands and their role.","a":["Paired seminal vesicles, one prostate gland, paired bulbourethral (Cowper's) glands.","Their secretions form seminal plasma.","Seminal plasma is rich in fructose, calcium and certain enzymes.","Bulbourethral secretion also lubricates the penis."],"kn":"ಶುಕ್ರಕೋಶಗಳು, ಪ್ರಾಸ್ಟೇಟ್, ಕೌಪರ್ ಗ್ರಂಥಿಗಳು — ವೀರ್ಯ ದ್ರವ.","hi":"शुक्राशय, प्रोस्टेट, काउपर ग्रंथियाँ — वीर्य द्रव।"},{"mk":2,"q":"What is parturition? Which hormone helps it?","a":["Parturition is the process of delivery of the foetus (childbirth).","It is induced by a neuroendocrine mechanism; oxytocin causes strong uterine contractions."],"kn":"ಹೆರಿಗೆ; ಆಕ್ಸಿಟೋಸಿನ್.","hi":"प्रसव; ऑक्सीटोसिन।"},{"mk":2,"q":"What is colostrum? Why is it important?","a":["The milk produced in the first few days after delivery.","It contains antibodies (IgA) that give resistance to the newborn."],"kn":"ಮೊದಲ ಹಾಲು; ಪ್ರತಿಕಾಯಗಳು (IgA) ಇರುತ್ತವೆ.","hi":"पहला दूध; इसमें एंटीबॉडी (IgA) होती हैं।"}],"dia":[{"n":"Sectional view of seminiferous tubule","l":["Spermatogonia","Primary spermatocyte","Spermatids","Sperms","Sertoli cells","Interstitial (Leydig) cells"]},{"n":"Section of ovary","l":["Primary follicle","Secondary follicle","Tertiary follicle","Graafian follicle","Ovum","Corpus luteum","Blood vessels"]},{"n":"Structure of a sperm","l":["Acrosome","Head with nucleus","Neck","Middle piece with mitochondria","Tail"]}],"facts":["Fertilisation occurs in the ampulla of the fallopian tube.","Leydig cells secrete testosterone.","Sertoli cells nourish developing sperms.","Graafian follicle releases the ovum (ovulation) on about day 14.","Corpus luteum secretes progesterone.","hCG is secreted only during pregnancy.","Embryo implants at the blastocyst stage.","Human pregnancy lasts about 9 months."],"trick":["Menstrual cycle \"M-F-O-L\" = Menstrual, Follicular, Ovulatory, Luteal.","Leydig = Libido hormone (testosterone); Sertoli = Servant (nurse cells)."],"bp":[2,0,1,1]},{"ch":3,"t":"Reproductive Health","m":"6","plan":"Short and easy. Learn the contraception table (natural, barrier, IUD, pills, surgical), MTP, STIs and ART names — almost every line is a 1- or 2-mark answer.","kn":"ಸುರಕ್ಷಿತ ಸಂತಾನೋತ್ಪತ್ತಿ ಆರೋಗ್ಯ: ಗರ್ಭನಿರೋಧಕ ವಿಧಾನಗಳು, MTP, ಲೈಂಗಿಕ ರೋಗಗಳು ಮತ್ತು ಬಂಜೆತನಕ್ಕೆ ಚಿಕಿತ್ಸೆ (ART).","hi":"सुरक्षित प्रजनन स्वास्थ्य: गर्भनिरोधक उपाय, MTP, यौन संचारित रोग और बांझपन का इलाज (ART)।","qs":[{"mk":5,"q":"Explain the different methods of contraception.","a":["Natural methods: periodic abstinence, withdrawal (coitus interruptus), lactational amenorrhoea.","Barrier methods: condoms (male and female), diaphragms, cervical caps, vaults — stop sperm meeting the ovum.","IUDs: non-medicated (Lippes loop), copper-releasing (CuT, Cu7, Multiload 375), hormone-releasing (Progestasert, LNG-20).","Oral pills: progestogens or progestogen-oestrogen combinations; inhibit ovulation and implantation (e.g. Saheli).","Injections / implants of the same hormones.","Surgical methods (sterilisation): vasectomy in males, tubectomy in females."],"kn":"ನೈಸರ್ಗಿಕ, ತಡೆ, IUD, ಮಾತ್ರೆ, ಚುಚ್ಚುಮದ್ದು, ಶಸ್ತ್ರಚಿಕಿತ್ಸೆ — 6 ವಿಧ.","hi":"प्राकृतिक, रोध, IUD, गोली, इंजेक्शन, शल्य — 6 प्रकार।"},{"mk":3,"q":"Write the aims / features of the RCH programme.","a":["RCH = Reproductive and Child Health care programme.","Creates awareness about reproduction-related aspects.","Provides facilities and support for a reproductively healthy society.","Includes sex education, family planning, care of mother and baby, and control of STIs."],"kn":"ಸಂತಾನೋತ್ಪತ್ತಿ ಮತ್ತು ಮಕ್ಕಳ ಆರೋಗ್ಯ ಕಾರ್ಯಕ್ರಮ.","hi":"प्रजनन एवं शिशु स्वास्थ्य कार्यक्रम।"},{"mk":3,"q":"What is MTP? When is it considered safe?","a":["MTP = Medical Termination of Pregnancy (intentional abortion before full term).","Legalised in India in 1971 (MTP Act) with conditions.","Relatively safe during the first trimester (up to 12 weeks).","Misuse for female foeticide is illegal."],"kn":"ಗರ್ಭಪಾತ; ಮೊದಲ 12 ವಾರ ಸುರಕ್ಷಿತ.","hi":"गर्भ समापन; पहले 12 हफ़्ते सुरक्षित।"},{"mk":3,"q":"Name any six sexually transmitted infections (STIs). How can they be prevented?","a":["Gonorrhoea, syphilis, genital herpes, chlamydiasis, genital warts, trichomoniasis, hepatitis-B, HIV/AIDS.","Prevention: avoid sex with unknown / multiple partners.","Always use condoms.","See a doctor early for any doubt."],"kn":"ಗೊನೋರಿಯಾ, ಸಿಫಿಲಿಸ್, ಹರ್ಪಿಸ್… ತಡೆ: ಕಾಂಡೋಮ್, ಒಬ್ಬ ಸಂಗಾತಿ.","hi":"गोनोरिया, सिफलिस, हर्पीज़… बचाव: कंडोम, एक साथी।"},{"mk":3,"q":"Explain any three assisted reproductive technologies (ART).","a":["IVF–ET (test tube baby): fertilisation outside the body, embryo transferred to the uterus.","ZIFT: zygote / early embryo (up to 8 blastomeres) transferred into the fallopian tube; IUT: embryo with more than 8 blastomeres into the uterus.","GIFT: ovum from a donor transferred into the fallopian tube.","ICSI: sperm injected directly into the ovum.","AI / IUI: semen introduced into the vagina or uterus."],"kn":"IVF, ZIFT, GIFT, ICSI, AI — ಬಂಜೆತನಕ್ಕೆ ಚಿಕಿತ್ಸೆ.","hi":"IVF, ZIFT, GIFT, ICSI, AI — बांझपन का इलाज।"},{"mk":2,"q":"What is amniocentesis? Why is it banned for sex determination?","a":["Test of amniotic fluid to detect genetic disorders in the foetus.","It is misused to find the sex of the foetus, leading to female foeticide, so it is banned for that purpose."],"kn":"ಆಮ್ನಿಯೋಟಿಕ್ ದ್ರವ ಪರೀಕ್ಷೆ; ಲಿಂಗ ಪತ್ತೆಗೆ ನಿಷೇಧ.","hi":"उल्ब द्रव जाँच; लिंग जाँच पर रोक।"}],"dia":[{"n":"IUD — Copper T (optional, simple sketch)","l":["Copper wire","Plastic T-frame","Thread"]}],"facts":["Saheli is a once-a-week non-steroidal oral pill (CDRI, Lucknow).","Copper ions in CuT reduce sperm motility.","Vasectomy cuts the vas deferens; tubectomy cuts the fallopian tube.","MTP Act in India: 1971.","Lactational amenorrhoea is effective up to 6 months after delivery.","IVF baby is called a test-tube baby."],"trick":["IUD types \"N-C-H\" = Non-medicated, Copper, Hormone.","ZIFT = Zygote Into Fallopian Tube; GIFT = Gamete Into Fallopian Tube."],"bp":[1,1,1,0]},{"ch":4,"t":"Principles of Inheritance and Variation","m":"13","plan":"Practise monohybrid and dihybrid crosses with Punnett squares — a neat cross is a sure 5 marks. Then learn sex determination and 3 disorders.","kn":"ತಂದೆ-ತಾಯಿಯಿಂದ ಮಕ್ಕಳಿಗೆ ಗುಣಗಳು ಹೇಗೆ ಬರುತ್ತವೆ — ಮೆಂಡೆಲ್‌ನ ನಿಯಮಗಳು, ಲಿಂಗ ನಿರ್ಧಾರ ಮತ್ತು ಆನುವಂಶಿಕ ರೋಗಗಳು.","hi":"माता-पिता से बच्चों में गुण कैसे आते हैं — मेंडल के नियम, लिंग निर्धारण और आनुवंशिक रोग।","qs":[{"mk":5,"q":"Explain a monohybrid cross with an example and state the law of segregation.","a":["Cross between pure tall (TT) and pure dwarf (tt) pea plants.","F1: all tall (Tt) — tall is dominant.","F1 selfed (Tt × Tt) → F2 by Punnett square: TT, Tt, Tt, tt.","Phenotypic ratio 3 tall : 1 dwarf; genotypic ratio 1 TT : 2 Tt : 1 tt.","Law of segregation: the two alleles of a gene separate during gamete formation, so each gamete gets only one allele.","Draw the Punnett square."],"kn":"TT × tt → F1 Tt → F2 3:1 (ಲಕ್ಷಣ), 1:2:1 (ಜೀನ್).","hi":"TT × tt → F1 Tt → F2 3:1 (लक्षण), 1:2:1 (जीन)।"},{"mk":5,"q":"Explain a dihybrid cross and the law of independent assortment.","a":["Cross: round yellow (RRYY) × wrinkled green (rryy).","F1: all round yellow (RrYy).","F1 forms 4 types of gametes: RY, Ry, rY, ry.","F2 (16-box Punnett square) ratio 9 round yellow : 3 round green : 3 wrinkled yellow : 1 wrinkled green.","Law of independent assortment: when two pairs of traits are combined, alleles of one pair segregate independently of the other pair."],"kn":"RRYY × rryy → F2 9:3:3:1.","hi":"RRYY × rryy → F2 9:3:3:1।"},{"mk":5,"q":"Explain sex determination in humans.","a":["Humans have XY type of sex determination.","Female: 22 pairs autosomes + XX; male: 22 pairs autosomes + XY.","Female produces only one type of egg (X) — homogametic.","Male produces two types of sperm: X and Y (50% each) — heterogametic.","Egg + X sperm → XX (girl); egg + Y sperm → XY (boy).","So the sex of the baby is decided by the father's sperm."],"kn":"ತಂದೆಯ X ಅಥವಾ Y ವೀರ್ಯದಿಂದ ಮಗುವಿನ ಲಿಂಗ ನಿರ್ಧಾರ.","hi":"पिता के X या Y शुक्राणु से बच्चे का लिंग तय होता है।"},{"mk":3,"q":"What is incomplete dominance? Explain with an example.","a":["F1 shows a phenotype in between the two parents.","Example: snapdragon (Antirrhinum) — red (RR) × white (rr) → F1 pink (Rr).","F2: 1 red : 2 pink : 1 white — phenotypic and genotypic ratios are the same."],"kn":"ಕೆಂಪು × ಬಿಳಿ → ಗುಲಾಬಿ (ಸ್ನ್ಯಾಪ್‌ಡ್ರ್ಯಾಗನ್), F2 1:2:1.","hi":"लाल × सफ़ेद → गुलाबी (स्नैपड्रैगन), F2 1:2:1।"},{"mk":3,"q":"Explain co-dominance with the ABO blood group example.","a":["Both alleles express fully in the hybrid.","ABO blood group is controlled by gene I with 3 alleles: IA, IB, i.","IA and IB are co-dominant → blood group AB (both A and B antigens).","i is recessive: IAi = A, IBi = B, ii = O.","There are 6 genotypes and 4 phenotypes (blood groups)."],"kn":"IA, IB ಎರಡೂ ವ್ಯಕ್ತ → AB ರಕ್ತಗುಂಪು.","hi":"IA, IB दोनों व्यक्त → AB रक्त समूह।"},{"mk":3,"q":"Write the cause and symptoms of Down's syndrome / Klinefelter / Turner syndrome.","a":["Down's syndrome: extra copy of chromosome 21 (trisomy 21); short, round head, furrowed tongue, mental retardation.","Klinefelter syndrome: XXY male (47); tall, sterile, develops breasts (gynaecomastia).","Turner syndrome: XO female (45); sterile, rudimentary ovaries, short stature."],"kn":"ಡೌನ್ = 21 ಟ್ರೈಸೋಮಿ; ಕ್ಲೈನ್‌ಫೆಲ್ಟರ್ = XXY; ಟರ್ನರ್ = XO.","hi":"डाउन = ट्राइसोमी 21; क्लाइनफेल्टर = XXY; टर्नर = XO।"},{"mk":2,"q":"Why is haemophilia more common in males? / What is a test cross?","a":["Haemophilia is X-linked recessive; males have only one X, so one faulty allele causes the disease.","Test cross: crossing an F1 (dominant phenotype) with the recessive parent to find its genotype (ratio 1:1 if heterozygous)."],"kn":"ಗಂಡಿಗೆ ಒಂದೇ X; ಪರೀಕ್ಷಾ ಸಂಕರ = ಅಪ್ರಬಲ ಪೋಷಕದೊಂದಿಗೆ ಸಂಕರ.","hi":"पुरुष में एक ही X; परीक्षार्थ संकरण = अप्रभावी जनक से संकरण।"}],"dia":[{"n":"Punnett square — monohybrid cross (TT × tt, F1 selfed)","l":["Gametes T, t on both sides","TT","Tt","Tt","tt","Ratio 3:1"]},{"n":"Punnett square — dihybrid cross (RrYy × RrYy)","l":["Gametes RY, Ry, rY, ry","16 boxes","9:3:3:1"]}],"facts":["Mendel worked on garden pea (Pisum sativum) and studied 7 pairs of traits.","Phenotypic ratio of a monohybrid cross: 3:1.","Dihybrid ratio: 9:3:3:1.","Test-cross ratio (monohybrid, heterozygous): 1:1.","Sickle-cell anaemia: GAG → GUG, glutamic acid replaced by valine.","Phenylketonuria is an autosomal recessive disorder.","Colour blindness and haemophilia are X-linked recessive.","Morgan worked on Drosophila (fruit fly)."],"trick":["\"3-1, 1-2-1, 9-3-3-1\" — say it daily; most crosses end in one of these.","Turner = only One X (XO); Klinefelter = Klein + extra X (XXY)."],"bp":[1,1,0,2]},{"ch":5,"t":"Molecular Basis of Inheritance","m":"13","plan":"Concept chapter. Secure the lac operon, Meselson–Stahl, Hershey–Chase and features of the genetic code — each is a standard 5-mark answer with a fixed set of points.","kn":"DNA ಆನುವಂಶಿಕ ವಸ್ತು ಎಂದು ಹೇಗೆ ಸಾಬೀತಾಯಿತು, DNA ನಕಲು ಹೇಗೆ, DNA → RNA → ಪ್ರೋಟೀನ್, ಮತ್ತು ಜೀನ್‌ಗಳ ನಿಯಂತ್ರಣ (ಲ್ಯಾಕ್ ಒಪೆರಾನ್).","hi":"DNA आनुवंशिक पदार्थ है यह कैसे साबित हुआ, DNA की प्रतिकृति, DNA → RNA → प्रोटीन, और जीन नियंत्रण (लैक ओपेरॉन)।","qs":[{"mk":5,"q":"Explain the lac operon.","a":["Operon in E. coli for lactose metabolism (Jacob and Monod).","Parts: regulator gene (i), promoter (p), operator (o) and 3 structural genes z, y, a.","z → β-galactosidase, y → permease, a → transacetylase.","Without lactose: the i gene makes a repressor that binds the operator → RNA polymerase is blocked → genes OFF.","With lactose (inducer): lactose binds the repressor → repressor cannot bind the operator → transcription occurs → genes ON.","This is negative regulation of an inducible operon. Draw both states."],"kn":"ಲ್ಯಾಕ್ಟೋಸ್ ಇಲ್ಲ → ರಿಪ್ರೆಸರ್ ಬಂಧನ → OFF; ಲ್ಯಾಕ್ಟೋಸ್ ಇದೆ → ON.","hi":"लैक्टोज़ नहीं → रिप्रेसर बंधता → OFF; लैक्टोज़ है → ON।"},{"mk":5,"q":"Describe the Meselson and Stahl experiment.","a":["Proved that DNA replication is semi-conservative.","E. coli grown in ¹⁵NH₄Cl for many generations → heavy DNA (¹⁵N–¹⁵N).","Cells shifted to ¹⁴NH₄Cl medium.","DNA separated by CsCl density-gradient centrifugation.","After 20 min (1 generation): all DNA hybrid / intermediate (¹⁵N–¹⁴N).","After 40 min (2 generations): equal hybrid and light (¹⁴N–¹⁴N) DNA.","This matches semi-conservative replication."],"kn":"¹⁵N → ¹⁴N; ಅರೆ-ಸಂರಕ್ಷಕ ನಕಲು ಸಾಬೀತು.","hi":"¹⁵N → ¹⁴N; अर्ध-संरक्षी प्रतिकृति सिद्ध।"},{"mk":5,"q":"Explain the Hershey–Chase experiment.","a":["Proved that DNA is the genetic material (1952).","Bacteriophages grown with radioactive ³²P (labels DNA) and ³⁵S (labels protein) separately.","Labelled phages allowed to infect E. coli.","Blending removed the phage coats; centrifugation separated bacteria from viruses.","Bacteria infected with ³²P phage were radioactive; with ³⁵S phage were not.","So DNA, not protein, enters the bacteria — DNA is the genetic material."],"kn":"³²P (DNA) ಬ್ಯಾಕ್ಟೀರಿಯಾ ಒಳಗೆ ಹೋಯಿತು → DNA ಆನುವಂಶಿಕ ವಸ್ತು.","hi":"³²P (DNA) बैक्टीरिया के अंदर गया → DNA आनुवंशिक पदार्थ।"},{"mk":5,"q":"Write the salient features of the genetic code.","a":["Triplet: 3 nucleotides code for one amino acid; 64 codons.","61 codons code for amino acids; 3 (UAA, UAG, UGA) are stop codons.","AUG is the start codon and codes for methionine.","Unambiguous and specific: one codon → one amino acid.","Degenerate: some amino acids have more than one codon.","Read continuously, without commas.","Nearly universal."],"kn":"ತ್ರಿವಳಿ, 64 ಕೋಡಾನ್, AUG ಆರಂಭ, 3 ನಿಲುಗಡೆ, ಸಾರ್ವತ್ರಿಕ.","hi":"त्रिक, 64 कोडॉन, AUG आरंभ, 3 समापन, सार्वत्रिक।"},{"mk":5,"q":"Write the salient features of the Watson–Crick model of DNA.","a":["Two polynucleotide chains — double helix.","Sugar–phosphate backbone outside; bases inside.","Chains are antiparallel (5′→3′ and 3′→5′).","Complementary base pairing: A=T (2 H-bonds), G≡C (3 H-bonds).","Right-handed coil; pitch 3.4 nm; about 10 bp per turn; 0.34 nm between base pairs."],"kn":"ದ್ವಿಸುರುಳಿ, ವಿರುದ್ಧ ದಿಕ್ಕಿನ ಸರಪಳಿಗಳು, A=T, G≡C, 3.4 nm.","hi":"द्विकुंडली, प्रतिसमांतर, A=T, G≡C, 3.4 nm।"},{"mk":3,"q":"Write the steps / applications of DNA fingerprinting.","a":["DNA isolated and cut with restriction enzymes.","Fragments separated by electrophoresis and blotted (Southern blot).","Hybridised with labelled VNTR probes and detected by autoradiography.","Uses: forensic (crime) tests, paternity disputes, population studies.","Developed by Alec Jeffreys."],"kn":"VNTR ಆಧಾರಿತ; ಅಪರಾಧ, ತಂದೆತನ ಪತ್ತೆಗೆ.","hi":"VNTR आधारित; अपराध, पितृत्व जाँच में।"},{"mk":3,"q":"Write any three goals of the Human Genome Project.","a":["Identify all the genes (about 20,000–25,000) in human DNA.","Determine the sequence of the 3 billion base pairs.","Store this information in databases and improve tools for analysis.","Address the ethical, legal and social issues (ELSI)."],"kn":"ಎಲ್ಲಾ ಜೀನ್‌ಗಳು ಮತ್ತು 3 ಬಿಲಿಯನ್ ಬೇಸ್ ಜೋಡಿ ಅನುಕ್ರಮ ತಿಳಿಯುವುದು.","hi":"सभी जीन और 3 अरब बेस जोड़ों का अनुक्रम जानना।"},{"mk":2,"q":"What is transformation (Griffith)? / Define central dogma.","a":["Griffith: heat-killed S strain + live R strain → mouse died; R strain was transformed by a \"transforming principle\" (later shown to be DNA).","Central dogma: DNA → (transcription) → mRNA → (translation) → protein."],"kn":"R ಸ್ಟ್ರೈನ್ S ಆಗಿ ಬದಲಾವಣೆ; DNA → RNA → ಪ್ರೋಟೀನ್.","hi":"R स्ट्रेन का S में बदलना; DNA → RNA → प्रोटीन।"}],"dia":[{"n":"Lac operon (switched off and on)","l":["Regulator gene i","Promoter p","Operator o","Structural genes z, y, a","Repressor","Inducer (lactose)","RNA polymerase"]},{"n":"Meselson–Stahl results (CsCl tube bands)","l":["Heavy ¹⁵N band (generation 0)","Hybrid band (20 min)","Hybrid + light bands (40 min)"]}],"facts":["DNA replication is semi-conservative.","Okazaki fragments are formed on the lagging strand.","DNA ligase joins Okazaki fragments.","RNA polymerase II transcribes mRNA in eukaryotes.","Start codon AUG = methionine.","Stop codons: UAA, UAG, UGA.","Removal of introns and joining of exons = splicing.","Human genome has about 3 × 10⁹ base pairs."],"trick":["Stop codons: \"U Are Away, U Are Gone, U Go Away\" = UAA, UAG, UGA.","Lac operon genes \"z-y-a\" = β-galactosidase, permease, transacetylase (Zebra Yawns Again)."],"bp":[1,1,0,2]},{"ch":6,"t":"Evolution","m":"7","plan":"Learn the theory answers in order: origin of life → Miller–Urey → evidences → Darwin → Hardy–Weinberg. Draw the Miller–Urey apparatus neatly.","kn":"ಜೀವ ಹೇಗೆ ಹುಟ್ಟಿತು ಮತ್ತು ಜೀವಿಗಳು ಹೇಗೆ ಬದಲಾದವು — ಮಿಲ್ಲರ್ ಪ್ರಯೋಗ, ವಿಕಾಸದ ಸಾಕ್ಷ್ಯಗಳು, ಡಾರ್ವಿನ್ ಸಿದ್ಧಾಂತ ಮತ್ತು ಮಾನವ ವಿಕಾಸ.","hi":"जीवन कैसे शुरू हुआ और जीव कैसे बदले — मिलर प्रयोग, विकास के प्रमाण, डार्विन का सिद्धांत और मानव विकास।","qs":[{"mk":5,"q":"Describe the Miller–Urey experiment.","a":["Tested Oparin–Haldane's idea of chemical evolution (1953).","A closed flask had CH₄, NH₃, H₂ and water vapour (like the early earth's atmosphere).","Electric sparks were passed at about 800 °C (like lightning).","Vapours were cooled in a condenser and collected.","After a week, amino acids were found in the liquid.","This showed simple organic molecules can form from inorganic molecules."],"kn":"CH₄, NH₃, H₂, ನೀರು + ವಿದ್ಯುತ್ ಕಿಡಿ → ಅಮೈನೋ ಆಮ್ಲಗಳು.","hi":"CH₄, NH₃, H₂, जल + विद्युत चिंगारी → अमीनो अम्ल।"},{"mk":5,"q":"Explain Darwin's theory of natural selection.","a":["Organisms produce more offspring than can survive (over-production).","Resources are limited → struggle for existence.","Members of a species show variations; some are heritable.","Individuals with useful variations survive and reproduce more — survival of the fittest (fitness = reproductive fitness).","Over many generations, useful variations accumulate → new species form.","Example: industrial melanism in peppered moth."],"kn":"ಅತಿಯಾದ ಉತ್ಪಾದನೆ → ಹೋರಾಟ → ವ್ಯತ್ಯಾಸ → ಯೋಗ್ಯತಮರ ಉಳಿವು → ಹೊಸ ಪ್ರಭೇದ.","hi":"अति उत्पादन → संघर्ष → विभिन्नता → योग्यतम की उत्तरजीविता → नई जाति।"},{"mk":5,"q":"Explain the evidences of evolution.","a":["Palaeontological: fossils in rock layers show life forms changed over time.","Homologous organs: same structure, different function — divergent evolution (forelimbs of whale, bat, cheetah, human).","Analogous organs: different structure, same function — convergent evolution (wings of butterfly and bird).","Biochemical: similarity in proteins and genes.","Natural selection seen today: industrial melanism, antibiotic / pesticide resistance."],"kn":"ಪಳೆಯುಳಿಕೆ, ಸಮರೂಪಿ ಅಂಗ, ಸಮಕಾರ್ಯ ಅಂಗ, ಜೀವರಸಾಯನ ಸಾಕ್ಷ್ಯ.","hi":"जीवाश्म, समजात अंग, समरूप अंग, जैव-रासायनिक प्रमाण।"},{"mk":5,"q":"State the Hardy–Weinberg principle and the factors affecting it.","a":["Allele frequencies in a population stay constant from generation to generation (genetic equilibrium).","Equation: p² + 2pq + q² = 1 (p + q = 1).","Factors that disturb it: gene migration / gene flow.","Genetic drift (founder effect).","Mutation.","Genetic recombination.","Natural selection."],"kn":"p² + 2pq + q² = 1; 5 ಅಂಶಗಳು ಸಮತೋಲನ ಕೆಡಿಸುತ್ತವೆ.","hi":"p² + 2pq + q² = 1; 5 कारक संतुलन बिगाड़ते हैं।"},{"mk":3,"q":"What is adaptive radiation? Give an example.","a":["Evolution of different species from one ancestor in a given area, radiating to other habitats.","Example: Darwin's finches of the Galapagos (different beaks for different food).","Example: Australian marsupials."],"kn":"ಒಂದು ಪೂರ್ವಜದಿಂದ ಹಲವು ಪ್ರಭೇದಗಳು — ಡಾರ್ವಿನ್ ಫಿಂಚ್‌ಗಳು.","hi":"एक पूर्वज से कई जातियाँ — डार्विन की फिंच।"},{"mk":3,"q":"Write the order of human evolution.","a":["Dryopithecus / Ramapithecus (about 15 mya).","Australopithecines (about 2 mya) — used stone tools.","Homo habilis — first human-like being, brain 650–800 cc.","Homo erectus (1.5 mya) — brain 900 cc, ate meat.","Neanderthal man (1400 cc) → Homo sapiens (modern man)."],"kn":"ಡ್ರಯೋಪಿಥೆಕಸ್ → ಆಸ್ಟ್ರಲೋಪಿಥೆಕಸ್ → ಹೋಮೊ ಹ್ಯಾಬಿಲಿಸ್ → ಹೋಮೊ ಎರೆಕ್ಟಸ್ → ನಿಯಾಂಡರ್ತಾಲ್ → ಹೋಮೊ ಸೇಪಿಯನ್ಸ್.","hi":"ड्रायोपिथेकस → ऑस्ट्रेलोपिथेकस → होमो हैबिलिस → होमो इरेक्टस → निएंडरथल → होमो सेपियन्स।"},{"mk":2,"q":"Differentiate homologous and analogous organs.","a":["Homologous: same origin and structure, different function (forelimbs of mammals; thorns of Bougainvillea and tendrils of Cucurbita).","Analogous: different origin and structure, same function (eye of octopus and mammal; wings of butterfly and bird)."],"kn":"ಸಮರೂಪಿ = ಒಂದೇ ರಚನೆ; ಸಮಕಾರ್ಯ = ಒಂದೇ ಕಾರ್ಯ.","hi":"समजात = समान संरचना; समरूप = समान कार्य।"}],"dia":[{"n":"Miller–Urey apparatus","l":["Electrodes (spark)","Gases CH₄, NH₃, H₂, H₂O","Condenser","Boiling water","Water out / water in","Collected liquid with amino acids"]}],"facts":["Universe is about 20 billion years old; earth about 4.5 billion years.","Theory of chemical evolution: Oparin and Haldane.","Industrial melanism: peppered moth (Biston betularia).","Darwin travelled on HMS Beagle.","Lamarck: use and disuse of organs (giraffe's neck).","Mutation theory: Hugo de Vries (Oenothera).","Founder effect is a type of genetic drift.","Homo habilis brain: 650–800 cc."],"trick":["Hardy–Weinberg disturbers \"G-G-M-R-N\": Gene flow, Genetic drift, Mutation, Recombination, Natural selection.","HOmologous = same Origin; ANalogous = same ActioN."],"bp":[2,1,1,0]},{"ch":7,"t":"Human Health and Disease","m":"11","plan":"Write the Plasmodium and HIV cycles as numbered flow-charts. Then learn the immunity pairs (innate vs acquired, active vs passive) and the disease table.","kn":"ರೋಗಗಳು (ಮಲೇರಿಯಾ, ಟೈಫಾಯ್ಡ್, ಏಡ್ಸ್, ಕ್ಯಾನ್ಸರ್), ನಮ್ಮ ರೋಗನಿರೋಧಕ ಶಕ್ತಿ ಮತ್ತು ಮಾದಕ ವಸ್ತುಗಳ ದುಷ್ಪರಿಣಾಮ.","hi":"रोग (मलेरिया, टाइफ़ॉइड, एड्स, कैंसर), हमारी प्रतिरक्षा और नशीले पदार्थों के दुष्प्रभाव।","qs":[{"mk":5,"q":"Describe the life cycle of Plasmodium.","a":["Infected female Anopheles mosquito bites → sporozoites enter human blood.","Sporozoites multiply in liver cells.","They then attack red blood cells and multiply, rupturing RBCs.","Rupture releases haemozoin → chills and high fever every 3–4 days.","Gametocytes form in RBCs; a mosquito takes them in when it bites.","Fertilisation and development in the mosquito's gut; sporozoites move to its salivary glands, ready to infect again."],"kn":"ಸೊಳ್ಳೆ → ಯಕೃತ್ತು → RBC → ಹೆಮೊಜೊಯಿನ್ ಜ್ವರ → ಗ್ಯಾಮಿಟೋಸೈಟ್ → ಸೊಳ್ಳೆ.","hi":"मच्छर → यकृत → RBC → हीमोज़ोइन बुखार → युग्मकजनक → मच्छर।"},{"mk":5,"q":"Explain how HIV causes AIDS.","a":["HIV is a retrovirus with RNA; it spreads through sexual contact, infected blood, shared needles and from mother to child.","HIV enters macrophages; reverse transcriptase makes viral DNA from its RNA.","Viral DNA joins the host DNA; macrophages keep producing viruses (HIV factory).","HIV then attacks helper T-lymphocytes (TH cells) and multiplies.","TH cell number falls → immunity drops → person gets infections like TB and fungal infections.","Diagnosis: ELISA. No cure; antiretroviral drugs prolong life."],"kn":"HIV → ಮ್ಯಾಕ್ರೋಫೇಜ್ → TH ಕೋಶಗಳು ನಾಶ → ರೋಗನಿರೋಧಕ ಶಕ್ತಿ ಕುಸಿತ.","hi":"HIV → मैक्रोफेज → TH कोशिकाएँ नष्ट → प्रतिरक्षा कम।"},{"mk":5,"q":"Describe the structure of an antibody molecule.","a":["Antibody is a Y-shaped protein (immunoglobulin).","Made of 4 peptide chains: 2 heavy chains and 2 light chains (H₂L₂).","Chains are joined by disulphide bonds.","Tips of the arms have antigen-binding sites.","Produced by B-lymphocytes.","Types: IgA, IgM, IgE, IgG. Draw the labelled Y diagram."],"kn":"Y ಆಕಾರ, 2 ಭಾರಿ + 2 ಹಗುರ ಸರಪಳಿ, ಪ್ರತಿಜನಕ ಬಂಧನ ಸ್ಥಳ.","hi":"Y आकार, 2 भारी + 2 हल्की श्रृंखला, प्रतिजन बंधन स्थल।"},{"mk":3,"q":"What are the four barriers of innate immunity?","a":["Physical barriers: skin, mucus coating of respiratory, digestive and urinogenital tracts.","Physiological barriers: stomach acid, saliva, tears.","Cellular barriers: neutrophils, monocytes, NK cells, macrophages.","Cytokine barriers: interferons protect uninfected cells from viruses."],"kn":"ಭೌತಿಕ, ಶಾರೀರಿಕ, ಕೋಶೀಯ, ಸೈಟೊಕೈನ್ ತಡೆಗಳು.","hi":"भौतिक, कायिक, कोशिकीय, साइटोकाइन रोध।"},{"mk":3,"q":"Differentiate active and passive immunity.","a":["Active: body makes its own antibodies after exposure to an antigen (infection or vaccine); slow but long-lasting.","Passive: ready-made antibodies are given (colostrum, antitoxin injection); quick but short-lived.","Example of active: vaccination; passive: anti-tetanus serum, IgA in colostrum."],"kn":"ಸಕ್ರಿಯ = ದೇಹವೇ ಪ್ರತಿಕಾಯ ಮಾಡುತ್ತದೆ; ನಿಷ್ಕ್ರಿಯ = ಸಿದ್ಧ ಪ್ರತಿಕಾಯ ನೀಡುವುದು.","hi":"सक्रिय = शरीर स्वयं एंटीबॉडी बनाता है; निष्क्रिय = तैयार एंटीबॉडी देना।"},{"mk":3,"q":"Name the primary and secondary lymphoid organs.","a":["Primary: bone marrow and thymus — lymphocytes are formed and mature here.","Secondary: spleen, lymph nodes, tonsils, Peyer's patches, appendix, MALT — lymphocytes meet antigens here."],"kn":"ಪ್ರಾಥಮಿಕ: ಮಜ್ಜೆ, ಥೈಮಸ್; ದ್ವಿತೀಯ: ಪ್ಲೀಹ, ದುಗ್ಧಗ್ರಂಥಿ…","hi":"प्राथमिक: अस्थि मज्जा, थाइमस; द्वितीयक: प्लीहा, लसीका ग्रंथियाँ…"},{"mk":2,"q":"Name the cause and one symptom of typhoid / pneumonia / amoebiasis / ascariasis.","a":["Typhoid: Salmonella typhi — high fever; Widal test confirms.","Pneumonia: Streptococcus pneumoniae / Haemophilus influenzae — lungs fill with fluid.","Amoebiasis: Entamoeba histolytica — constipation, abdominal pain, mucus in stool; housefly is the carrier.","Ascariasis: Ascaris (roundworm) — internal bleeding, muscular pain, fever."],"kn":"ಟೈಫಾಯ್ಡ್ – ಸಾಲ್ಮೊನೆಲ್ಲಾ; ನ್ಯುಮೋನಿಯಾ – ಸ್ಟ್ರೆಪ್ಟೊಕಾಕಸ್…","hi":"टाइफ़ॉइड – साल्मोनेला; निमोनिया – स्ट्रेप्टोकोकस…"}],"dia":[{"n":"Life cycle of Plasmodium","l":["Mosquito bite (sporozoites)","Liver cells","RBC stage","Gametocytes","Mosquito gut (fertilisation)","Salivary gland (sporozoites)"]},{"n":"Antibody molecule","l":["Heavy chain","Light chain","Antigen-binding site","Disulphide bonds"]}],"facts":["Widal test confirms typhoid.","ELISA is used to diagnose AIDS.","Haemozoin causes the chill and fever in malaria.","Malaria is spread by the female Anopheles mosquito.","Interferons are cytokine barriers.","Cancer cells lose contact inhibition.","Opioids bind to receptors in the CNS; heroin is diacetylmorphine (smack).","Cannabinoids come from Cannabis sativa."],"trick":["Plasmodium path \"M-L-R-G-M\" = Mosquito, Liver, RBC, Gametocyte, Mosquito.","Antibody \"2H + 2L = H₂L₂, shaped like a Y\"."],"bp":[3,0,1,1]},{"ch":8,"t":"Microbes in Human Welfare","m":"7","plan":"Easy scoring chapter. Learn the biogas plant diagram, sewage treatment steps and the \"microbe → product\" table; most questions ask for names.","kn":"ಸೂಕ್ಷ್ಮಜೀವಿಗಳು ನಮಗೆ ಹೇಗೆ ಉಪಯೋಗ — ಮೊಸರು, ಬ್ರೆಡ್, ಔಷಧ, ಒಳಚರಂಡಿ ಶುದ್ಧೀಕರಣ, ಜೈವಿಕ ಅನಿಲ, ಜೈವಿಕ ಗೊಬ್ಬರ ಮತ್ತು ಜೈವಿಕ ಕೀಟನಾಶಕ.","hi":"सूक्ष्मजीव हमारे कैसे काम आते हैं — दही, ब्रेड, दवाइयाँ, सीवेज उपचार, बायोगैस, जैव उर्वरक और जैव नियंत्रण।","qs":[{"mk":5,"q":"Explain the working of a biogas plant.","a":["Biogas is a mixture of mainly methane, with CO₂ and H₂S.","Cattle dung (gobar) slurry is fed into a concrete tank (digester) 10–15 feet deep.","Methanogens (e.g. Methanobacterium) present in the dung break it down anaerobically.","A floating cover rises as gas is produced.","Gas is taken out through an outlet pipe for cooking and lighting.","Spent slurry is removed and used as manure. Developed by IARI and KVIC."],"kn":"ಸಗಣಿ + ಮೆಥನೋಜೆನ್‌ಗಳು (ಆಮ್ಲಜನಕ ಇಲ್ಲದೆ) → ಮೀಥೇನ್ ಅನಿಲ.","hi":"गोबर + मेथेनोजन (बिना ऑक्सीजन) → मीथेन गैस।"},{"mk":5,"q":"Explain sewage treatment.","a":["Primary treatment: physical removal of particles by filtration and sedimentation → primary sludge.","Secondary (biological) treatment: effluent passed to aeration tanks; aerobic microbes form flocs and reduce BOD.","When BOD falls, effluent goes to a settling tank; flocs settle as activated sludge.","Part of the activated sludge is pumped back as inoculum.","Rest goes to anaerobic sludge digesters where bacteria produce biogas (methane, H₂S, CO₂).","Treated effluent is released into rivers."],"kn":"ಪ್ರಾಥಮಿಕ (ಭೌತಿಕ) → ದ್ವಿತೀಯ (ಸೂಕ್ಷ್ಮಜೀವಿ, ಫ್ಲಾಕ್‌ಗಳು) → ಸಕ್ರಿಯ ಕೆಸರು → ಜೈವಿಕ ಅನಿಲ.","hi":"प्राथमिक (भौतिक) → द्वितीयक (सूक्ष्मजीव, फ़्लॉक) → सक्रिय आपंक → बायोगैस।"},{"mk":5,"q":"What are biofertilisers? Give examples.","a":["Organisms that enrich the nutrient quality of the soil.","Bacteria: Rhizobium in root nodules of legumes fixes nitrogen.","Free-living bacteria Azotobacter and Azospirillum fix nitrogen.","Fungi: mycorrhiza (Glomus) absorbs phosphorus for the plant.","Cyanobacteria: Anabaena, Nostoc, Oscillatoria fix nitrogen in paddy fields."],"kn":"ಮಣ್ಣಿನ ಫಲವತ್ತತೆ ಹೆಚ್ಚಿಸುವ ಸೂಕ್ಷ್ಮಜೀವಿಗಳು — ರೈಜೋಬಿಯಂ, ಅನಾಬೀನಾ.","hi":"मिट्टी की उर्वरता बढ़ाने वाले सूक्ष्मजीव — राइज़ोबियम, एनाबीना।"},{"mk":3,"q":"Name the microbes used in household / industrial products.","a":["Curd: Lactobacillus (LAB) — also increases vitamin B₁₂.","Bread / beer / wine: Saccharomyces cerevisiae (baker's / brewer's yeast).","Swiss cheese: Propionibacterium sharmanii (large holes).","Citric acid: Aspergillus niger; acetic acid: Acetobacter aceti; lactic acid: Lactobacillus.","Penicillin: Penicillium notatum (Alexander Fleming)."],"kn":"ಮೊಸರು – ಲ್ಯಾಕ್ಟೋಬ್ಯಾಸಿಲಸ್; ಬ್ರೆಡ್ – ಯೀಸ್ಟ್…","hi":"दही – लैक्टोबैसिलस; ब्रेड – यीस्ट…"},{"mk":3,"q":"What are biocontrol agents? Give examples.","a":["Biological methods to control plant diseases and pests instead of chemicals.","Ladybird beetle eats aphids; dragonflies eat mosquitoes.","Bacillus thuringiensis (Bt) kills caterpillars.","Trichoderma (fungus) controls plant pathogens.","Baculoviruses (Nucleopolyhedrovirus) kill insects."],"kn":"ರಾಸಾಯನಿಕದ ಬದಲು ಜೀವಿಗಳಿಂದ ಕೀಟ ನಿಯಂತ್ರಣ — Bt, ಟ್ರೈಕೋಡರ್ಮಾ.","hi":"रसायन के बजाय जीवों से कीट नियंत्रण — Bt, ट्राइकोडर्मा।"},{"mk":2,"q":"Name the source and use of: statins / streptokinase / cyclosporin A.","a":["Statins: Monascus purpureus (yeast) — lower blood cholesterol.","Streptokinase: Streptococcus — clot buster, removes clots in blood vessels.","Cyclosporin A: Trichoderma polysporum — immunosuppressive in organ transplant."],"kn":"ಸ್ಟ್ಯಾಟಿನ್ – ಕೊಲೆಸ್ಟ್ರಾಲ್ ಕಡಿಮೆ; ಸ್ಟ್ರೆಪ್ಟೋಕೈನೇಸ್ – ರಕ್ತಹೆಪ್ಪು ಕರಗಿಸುತ್ತದೆ.","hi":"स्टैटिन – कोलेस्ट्रॉल कम; स्ट्रेप्टोकाइनेज़ – थक्का घोलता है।"}],"dia":[{"n":"Biogas plant","l":["Dung + water slurry inlet","Digester","Floating gas holder / cover","Gas outlet","Sludge outlet (manure)"]}],"facts":["Biogas is mostly methane.","Methanogens live in the rumen of cattle.","BOD = amount of oxygen needed by microbes to oxidise organic matter in 1 litre of water.","High BOD means more pollution.","Penicillin was discovered by Alexander Fleming.","Baker's yeast: Saccharomyces cerevisiae.","Rhizobium forms root nodules in legumes.","Ganga Action Plan and Yamuna Action Plan treat sewage."],"trick":["Acids: \"Citric–Aspergillus, Acetic–Acetobacter, Lactic–Lactobacillus\" — the first letters match.","Biogas = \"Methane from Methanogens\"."],"bp":[2,1,1,0]},{"ch":9,"t":"Biotechnology: Principles and Processes","m":"7","plan":"Learn the tools (restriction enzymes, vectors, competent hosts) and the steps of recombinant DNA technology in order. Draw pBR322, PCR and the bioreactor.","kn":"ಒಂದು ಜೀವಿಯ ಉಪಯುಕ್ತ ಜೀನನ್ನು ಕತ್ತರಿಸಿ ಇನ್ನೊಂದು ಜೀವಿಗೆ ಸೇರಿಸುವ ವಿಧಾನ — ನಿರ್ಬಂಧಕ ಕಿಣ್ವಗಳು, ವಾಹಕಗಳು, PCR ಮತ್ತು ಜೈವಿಕ ರಿಯಾಕ್ಟರ್.","hi":"एक जीव का उपयोगी जीन काटकर दूसरे जीव में डालने की विधि — प्रतिबंधन एंज़ाइम, वाहक, PCR और बायोरिएक्टर।","qs":[{"mk":5,"q":"Explain the steps (processes) of recombinant DNA technology.","a":["Isolation of DNA: cells broken with lysozyme / cellulase / chitinase; RNA and protein removed with ribonuclease and protease; DNA precipitated with chilled ethanol.","Cutting DNA at specific sites with restriction enzymes; checked by agarose gel electrophoresis.","Amplification of the gene of interest by PCR.","Ligation of the gene into a vector with DNA ligase → recombinant DNA.","Insertion of recombinant DNA into a competent host cell (transformation).","Obtaining the foreign gene product, often in a bioreactor; downstream processing (separation, purification, formulation)."],"kn":"DNA ಬೇರ್ಪಡಿಸು → ಕತ್ತರಿಸು → PCR → ವಾಹಕಕ್ಕೆ ಜೋಡಿಸು → ಆತಿಥೇಯ ಕೋಶಕ್ಕೆ → ಉತ್ಪನ್ನ.","hi":"DNA अलग करो → काटो → PCR → वाहक से जोड़ो → परपोषी में डालो → उत्पाद।"},{"mk":5,"q":"Explain PCR (polymerase chain reaction).","a":["Used to make many copies of a gene in a test tube (Kary Mullis).","Denaturation: heating separates the two DNA strands.","Annealing: primers bind to the single strands.","Extension: Taq DNA polymerase (from Thermus aquaticus, heat-stable) adds nucleotides.","The cycle is repeated about 30 times; DNA is amplified about a billion times.","Uses: gene cloning, diagnosis of diseases (HIV), DNA fingerprinting."],"kn":"ವಿಘಟನೆ → ಪ್ರೈಮರ್ ಜೋಡಣೆ → ವಿಸ್ತರಣೆ (Taq ಪಾಲಿಮರೇಸ್); 30 ಚಕ್ರ.","hi":"विकृतीकरण → प्राइमर बंधन → विस्तार (Taq पॉलीमरेज़); 30 चक्र।"},{"mk":5,"q":"What are the features of a good cloning vector? (pBR322)","a":["Origin of replication (ori): where replication starts; controls the copy number.","Selectable marker: helps identify transformants, e.g. genes for resistance to ampicillin and tetracycline (ampR, tetR).","Cloning sites: unique recognition sites for restriction enzymes (e.g. BamHI, EcoRI, PstI).","Small size so it can easily enter host cells.","Insertional inactivation of a marker gene helps pick out recombinants (e.g. blue-white screening with lacZ)."],"kn":"ori, ಆಯ್ಕೆ ಗುರುತು (ampR, tetR), ಕ್ಲೋನಿಂಗ್ ಸ್ಥಳಗಳು.","hi":"ori, चयन चिह्नक (ampR, tetR), क्लोनिंग स्थल।"},{"mk":3,"q":"What are restriction enzymes? How are they named?","a":["Molecular scissors that cut DNA at specific palindromic sequences.","They make sticky ends that help join DNA pieces with DNA ligase.","Naming of EcoRI: E = genus Escherichia, co = species coli, R = strain RY13, I = first enzyme isolated from that strain.","Example palindrome: 5′-GAATTC-3′ / 3′-CTTAAG-5′."],"kn":"DNA ಕತ್ತರಿಗಳು; EcoRI ಹೆಸರಿನ ಅರ್ಥ.","hi":"DNA की कैंची; EcoRI नाम का अर्थ।"},{"mk":3,"q":"Explain gel electrophoresis.","a":["Technique to separate DNA fragments by size.","DNA is negatively charged, so it moves towards the anode in an agarose gel under an electric field.","Smaller fragments move farther.","DNA is stained with ethidium bromide and seen as orange bands under UV light.","Separated bands are cut out and extracted (elution)."],"kn":"ಚಿಕ್ಕ ತುಂಡುಗಳು ಹೆಚ್ಚು ದೂರ ಸಾಗುತ್ತವೆ; ಎಥಿಡಿಯಂ ಬ್ರೋಮೈಡ್ ಬಣ್ಣ.","hi":"छोटे टुकड़े अधिक दूर जाते हैं; एथिडियम ब्रोमाइड रंग।"},{"mk":2,"q":"What is a bioreactor? Name its types / parts.","a":["Large vessel (100–1000 litres) to grow cells and get products on a large scale.","Stirred-tank bioreactor has an agitator, oxygen supply (sparger), foam control, temperature and pH control, and sampling ports."],"kn":"ದೊಡ್ಡ ಪ್ರಮಾಣದಲ್ಲಿ ಉತ್ಪನ್ನ ತಯಾರಿಸುವ ಪಾತ್ರೆ.","hi":"बड़े पैमाने पर उत्पाद बनाने का पात्र।"},{"mk":2,"q":"What is a competent host? How is it made?","a":["A cell that can take up foreign DNA.","Bacterial cells are treated with divalent cations (calcium chloride) and then given a heat shock (ice → 42 °C → ice). Other ways: microinjection, gene gun (biolistics), disarmed pathogen vectors."],"kn":"ಹೊರ DNA ಸ್ವೀಕರಿಸುವ ಕೋಶ; CaCl₂ + ಉಷ್ಣ ಆಘಾತ.","hi":"बाहरी DNA ग्रहण करने वाली कोशिका; CaCl₂ + ताप आघात।"}],"dia":[{"n":"pBR322 plasmid","l":["ori","rop","ampR","tetR","BamHI","EcoRI","PstI","PvuI","HindIII","SalI"]},{"n":"PCR (one cycle)","l":["Denaturation","Annealing of primers","Extension by Taq polymerase"]}],"facts":["First recombinant DNA: Stanley Cohen and Herbert Boyer (1972).","Restriction enzymes are called molecular scissors.","DNA ligase is molecular glue.","Taq polymerase comes from Thermus aquaticus.","Ti plasmid of Agrobacterium tumefaciens is used as a vector for plants.","DNA is precipitated by chilled ethanol.","Ethidium bromide stains DNA (orange under UV).","Recombinants without colour in blue-white screening (insertional inactivation of lacZ)."],"trick":["PCR = \"D-A-E\": Denature, Anneal, Extend.","Vector must have \"O-S-C\": Ori, Selectable marker, Cloning sites."],"bp":[2,0,0,1]},{"ch":10,"t":"Biotechnology and its Applications","m":"6","plan":"Five fixed stories: Bt cotton, RNAi, human insulin, ADA gene therapy, transgenic animals. Learn each as 5–6 points; add GEAC and biopiracy for short answers.","kn":"ಜೈವತಂತ್ರಜ್ಞಾನದ ಉಪಯೋಗಗಳು — Bt ಹತ್ತಿ, ಕೀಟನಿರೋಧಕ ಸಸ್ಯಗಳು, ಮಾನವ ಇನ್ಸುಲಿನ್, ಜೀನ್ ಚಿಕಿತ್ಸೆ, ರೋಗ ಪತ್ತೆ ಮತ್ತು ಟ್ರಾನ್ಸ್‌ಜೆನಿಕ್ ಪ್ರಾಣಿಗಳು.","hi":"जैव प्रौद्योगिकी के उपयोग — Bt कपास, कीट-प्रतिरोधी पौधे, मानव इंसुलिन, जीन थेरेपी, रोग निदान और ट्रांसजेनिक जंतु।","qs":[{"mk":5,"q":"Explain Bt cotton and how Bt toxin works.","a":["Bt toxin comes from the bacterium Bacillus thuringiensis.","The bacterium makes the toxin as an inactive protoxin (crystal protein).","When an insect eats it, the alkaline pH of the insect gut makes it active.","Active toxin binds to midgut cells, makes pores → cells swell and burst → insect dies.","cry genes (cryIAc, cryIIAb control cotton bollworms; cryIAb controls corn borer) are put into cotton.","Bt cotton resists bollworms and needs less pesticide."],"kn":"ಕ್ರೈ ಜೀನ್ → ನಿಷ್ಕ್ರಿಯ ವಿಷ → ಕೀಟದ ಕ್ಷಾರೀಯ ಕರುಳಿನಲ್ಲಿ ಸಕ್ರಿಯ → ಕೀಟ ಸಾವು.","hi":"क्राई जीन → निष्क्रिय विष → कीट की क्षारीय आँत में सक्रिय → कीट मृत।"},{"mk":5,"q":"How is human insulin produced by genetic engineering?","a":["Insulin has two short polypeptide chains, A and B, joined by disulphide bridges.","In the body it is made as pro-insulin with an extra C-peptide.","Eli Lilly (1983) prepared two DNA sequences for chains A and B.","These were put into plasmids of E. coli to produce chains A and B separately.","The chains were extracted and joined by disulphide bonds → human insulin (Humulin).","No C-peptide step needed; no allergy as with animal insulin."],"kn":"A ಮತ್ತು B ಸರಪಳಿ ಜೀನ್‌ಗಳು E. coli ಯಲ್ಲಿ → ಡೈಸಲ್ಫೈಡ್ ಬಂಧದಿಂದ ಜೋಡಣೆ.","hi":"A और B श्रृंखला जीन E. coli में → डाइसल्फ़ाइड बंध से जोड़ना।"},{"mk":5,"q":"Explain gene therapy for ADA deficiency.","a":["ADA (adenosine deaminase) enzyme is needed for the immune system to work.","Deletion of the ADA gene causes ADA deficiency (immunodeficiency).","First gene therapy: 1990, a 4-year-old girl.","Lymphocytes taken from the patient's blood and grown in culture.","Functional ADA cDNA introduced into lymphocytes using a retroviral vector; cells returned to the patient.","Cells are not immortal, so treatment is repeated; a permanent cure needs the gene in bone-marrow cells at an early embryonic stage."],"kn":"ಲಿಂಫೋಸೈಟ್‌ಗಳಿಗೆ ಸರಿಯಾದ ADA ಜೀನ್ ಸೇರಿಸಿ ಮತ್ತೆ ರೋಗಿಗೆ ನೀಡುವುದು.","hi":"लिम्फोसाइट में सही ADA जीन डालकर रोगी को वापस देना।"},{"mk":3,"q":"Explain RNA interference (RNAi) to protect tobacco plants.","a":["Nematode Meloidogyne incognita infects tobacco roots.","Nematode-specific genes are introduced into the plant using Agrobacterium vectors.","The plant makes both sense and anti-sense RNA → double-stranded RNA.","dsRNA silences the specific mRNA of the nematode.","The parasite cannot survive → plant is protected."],"kn":"dsRNA ನೆಮಟೋಡ್‌ನ mRNA ನಿಶ್ಶಬ್ದಗೊಳಿಸುತ್ತದೆ.","hi":"dsRNA सूत्रकृमि के mRNA को निष्क्रिय करता है।"},{"mk":3,"q":"What are transgenic animals? Give their uses.","a":["Animals whose DNA is changed to carry and express a foreign gene.","Study of normal physiology and development.","Study of diseases (models for cancer, Alzheimer's, cystic fibrosis).","Biological products, e.g. Rosie the cow gave human α-lactalbumin-rich milk (1997).","Vaccine safety and chemical safety (toxicity) testing."],"kn":"ಹೊರ ಜೀನ್ ಹೊಂದಿರುವ ಪ್ರಾಣಿಗಳು — ರೋಸಿ ಹಸು.","hi":"बाहरी जीन वाले जंतु — रोज़ी गाय।"},{"mk":3,"q":"What is biopiracy? What is GEAC?","a":["Biopiracy: use of bio-resources or traditional knowledge of a country by companies without permission or payment (e.g. basmati rice, turmeric, neem patents).","GEAC (Genetic Engineering Appraisal Committee) in India decides on the validity of GM research and safety of releasing GM organisms for public use."],"kn":"ಅನುಮತಿ ಇಲ್ಲದೆ ಜೈವಸಂಪತ್ತಿನ ಬಳಕೆ; GEAC – GM ಸುರಕ್ಷತಾ ಸಮಿತಿ.","hi":"बिना अनुमति जैव संसाधन उपयोग; GEAC – GM सुरक्षा समिति।"},{"mk":2,"q":"What is Golden Rice? / Name two molecular diagnosis methods.","a":["Golden Rice is GM rice rich in vitamin A (β-carotene).","Molecular diagnosis: PCR and ELISA (ELISA is based on antigen–antibody interaction)."],"kn":"ವಿಟಮಿನ್ A ಹೆಚ್ಚಿನ ಅಕ್ಕಿ; PCR, ELISA.","hi":"विटामिन A युक्त चावल; PCR, ELISA।"}],"dia":[{"n":"Maturation of pro-insulin into insulin (simple sketch)","l":["A chain","B chain","C peptide","Disulphide bonds"]}],"facts":["Bt = Bacillus thuringiensis.","cry genes code for Bt toxin.","Humulin was made by Eli Lilly in 1983.","First gene therapy: 1990, ADA deficiency.","Rosie: first transgenic cow (1997).","RNAi protects tobacco from Meloidogyne incognita.","ELISA works on antigen–antibody interaction.","GEAC is the Indian GM regulatory body."],"trick":["Bt toxin: \"inactive in plant, active in insect gut (alkaline)\".","Insulin: \"A + B, no C\" — chains A and B made separately, C-peptide not needed."],"bp":[1,0,0,1]},{"ch":11,"t":"Organisms and Populations","m":"6","plan":"Learn the population interaction table (+/−) with one example each, the growth curves (J and S) and population attributes — a table answer earns full marks fast.","kn":"ಜೀವಿಗಳು ಪರಿಸರಕ್ಕೆ ಹೇಗೆ ಹೊಂದಿಕೊಳ್ಳುತ್ತವೆ, ಜನಸಂಖ್ಯೆ ಹೇಗೆ ಬೆಳೆಯುತ್ತದೆ ಮತ್ತು ಜೀವಿಗಳ ನಡುವೆ ಸಂಬಂಧಗಳು (ಸಹಜೀವನ, ಪರಾವಲಂಬನೆ, ಸ್ಪರ್ಧೆ…).","hi":"जीव पर्यावरण के अनुसार कैसे ढलते हैं, जनसंख्या कैसे बढ़ती है और जीवों के बीच संबंध (सहजीविता, परजीविता, प्रतिस्पर्धा…)।","qs":[{"mk":5,"q":"Explain the different types of population interactions with examples.","a":["Mutualism (+, +): lichen (fungus + alga); mycorrhiza; fig and wasp.","Competition (−, −): Abingdon tortoise and goats in Galapagos; Gause's principle.","Predation (+, −): tiger eats deer; prickly pear cactus controlled by a moth.","Parasitism (+, −): Cuscuta on hedge plants; lice on humans.","Commensalism (+, 0): orchid on mango branch; barnacles on whale; cattle egret and cattle.","Amensalism (−, 0): Penicillium inhibits bacteria."],"kn":"+,+ ಸಹಜೀವನ; −,− ಸ್ಪರ್ಧೆ; +,− ಬೇಟೆ/ಪರಾವಲಂಬನೆ; +,0 ಸಹಭೋಜಿತನ; −,0 ಅಮೆನ್ಸಲಿಸಂ.","hi":"+,+ सहोपकारिता; −,− प्रतिस्पर्धा; +,− परभक्षण/परजीविता; +,0 सहभोजिता; −,0 अंतरजातीय परजीविता।"},{"mk":5,"q":"Explain population growth models (exponential and logistic).","a":["Exponential growth: unlimited resources; J-shaped curve; dN/dt = rN.","Logistic growth: limited resources; S-shaped (sigmoid) curve.","Phases: lag phase → acceleration → deceleration → asymptote at carrying capacity (K).","Logistic equation: dN/dt = rN (K − N)/K (Verhulst–Pearl).","Logistic growth is more realistic in nature."],"kn":"J ಆಕಾರ = ಘಾತೀಯ; S ಆಕಾರ = ಲಾಜಿಸ್ಟಿಕ್, ಧಾರಣ ಸಾಮರ್ಥ್ಯ K.","hi":"J आकार = चरघातांकी; S आकार = संभार तंत्र, वहन क्षमता K।"},{"mk":3,"q":"Write any three attributes of a population.","a":["Birth rate (natality): births per 1000 individuals per year.","Death rate (mortality).","Sex ratio: ratio of females to males.","Age pyramid: shows pre-reproductive, reproductive and post-reproductive groups — expanding, stable or declining.","Population density (N)."],"kn":"ಜನನ ದರ, ಮರಣ ದರ, ಲಿಂಗ ಅನುಪಾತ, ವಯಸ್ಸಿನ ಪಿರಮಿಡ್.","hi":"जन्म दर, मृत्यु दर, लिंग अनुपात, आयु पिरामिड।"},{"mk":3,"q":"Write the factors that increase and decrease population density.","a":["Increase: natality (births) and immigration.","Decrease: mortality (deaths) and emigration.","Nt+1 = Nt + [(B + I) − (D + E)]."],"kn":"ಹೆಚ್ಚಳ: ಜನನ + ವಲಸೆ ಬರುವುದು; ಇಳಿಕೆ: ಮರಣ + ವಲಸೆ ಹೋಗುವುದು.","hi":"वृद्धि: जन्म + आप्रवासन; कमी: मृत्यु + उत्प्रवासन।"},{"mk":3,"q":"State Gause's competitive exclusion principle.","a":["Two closely related species competing for the same resources cannot live together indefinitely.","The competitively inferior one is eliminated in time.","Example: Abingdon tortoise disappeared after goats were introduced on the Galapagos island."],"kn":"ಒಂದೇ ಸಂಪನ್ಮೂಲಕ್ಕಾಗಿ ಎರಡು ಪ್ರಭೇದ ಸದಾ ಒಟ್ಟಿಗೆ ಬದುಕಲಾರವು.","hi":"एक ही संसाधन के लिए दो जातियाँ सदा साथ नहीं रह सकतीं।"},{"mk":2,"q":"What are brood parasitism and mutualism? Give one example each.","a":["Brood parasitism: the parasite lays eggs in the host's nest and the host incubates them — cuckoo (koel) in the crow's nest.","Mutualism: both species benefit — lichens (fungus + alga), mycorrhiza, fig and wasp."],"kn":"ಕೋಗಿಲೆ ಕಾಗೆಯ ಗೂಡಿನಲ್ಲಿ ಮೊಟ್ಟೆ; ಕಲ್ಲುಹೂವು.","hi":"कोयल कौए के घोंसले में अंडे; लाइकेन।"}],"dia":[{"n":"Population growth curves","l":["Time on X-axis","Population density on Y-axis","J-shaped (exponential): dN/dt = rN","S-shaped (logistic)","Carrying capacity K"]},{"n":"Age pyramids","l":["Expanding (triangle)","Stable (bell)","Declining (urn)","Pre-reproductive / reproductive / post-reproductive"]}],"facts":["Carrying capacity is shown by K.","r = intrinsic rate of natural increase.","Lichen is mutualism between fungus and alga.","Cuscuta is a parasitic plant without chlorophyll.","Cuckoo laying eggs in a crow's nest = brood parasitism.","Orchid on mango branch = commensalism.","Prickly pear cactus in Australia was controlled by a cactus-feeding moth.","Sex ratio and age pyramid are population attributes."],"trick":["Interactions by signs: \"++ Mutual, −− Compete, +− Predator/Parasite, +0 Commensal, −0 Amensal\".","\"J for Jump\" (unlimited) vs \"S for Stop at K\" (limited)."],"bp":[1,0,0,1]},{"ch":12,"t":"Ecosystem","m":"4","plan":"Small chapter, high return. Learn decomposition steps, energy flow (10% law) and the 3 ecological pyramids — draw the pyramids.","kn":"ಪರಿಸರ ವ್ಯವಸ್ಥೆಯಲ್ಲಿ ಶಕ್ತಿ ಹರಿವು, ಆಹಾರ ಸರಪಳಿ, ಉತ್ಪಾದಕತೆ, ಕೊಳೆಯುವಿಕೆ ಮತ್ತು ಪರಿಸರ ಪಿರಮಿಡ್‌ಗಳು.","hi":"पारितंत्र में ऊर्जा प्रवाह, खाद्य श्रृंखला, उत्पादकता, अपघटन और पारिस्थितिक पिरामिड।","qs":[{"mk":5,"q":"Explain the steps of decomposition.","a":["Decomposition: breaking down complex organic matter (detritus) into inorganic substances like CO₂, water and nutrients.","Fragmentation: detritivores (earthworm) break detritus into small particles.","Leaching: water-soluble nutrients go down into the soil and precipitate as unavailable salts.","Catabolism: bacterial and fungal enzymes break detritus into simpler inorganic substances.","Humification: forms dark, amorphous humus, resistant to microbes, decomposes very slowly.","Mineralisation: humus is degraded by microbes to release inorganic nutrients."],"kn":"ತುಂಡಾಗುವಿಕೆ → ಸೋರುವಿಕೆ → ಕ್ಯಾಟಬಾಲಿಸಮ್ → ಹ್ಯೂಮಿಫಿಕೇಶನ್ → ಖನಿಜೀಕರಣ.","hi":"विखंडन → निक्षालन → अपचय → ह्यूमीकरण → खनिजीकरण।"},{"mk":5,"q":"Explain energy flow in an ecosystem (10 percent law).","a":["Sun is the only source of energy; less than 50% of sunlight is PAR.","Plants capture only 2–10% of PAR — producers.","Energy flows in one direction: producers → herbivores → carnivores (unidirectional).","At each trophic level, only about 10% of energy passes to the next level (Lindeman's 10% law); the rest is lost as heat.","So food chains are short (3–4 levels).","Detritus food chain starts from dead organic matter."],"kn":"ಸೂರ್ಯ → ಉತ್ಪಾದಕ → ಸಸ್ಯಾಹಾರಿ → ಮಾಂಸಾಹಾರಿ; ಪ್ರತಿ ಹಂತಕ್ಕೆ 10% ಮಾತ್ರ.","hi":"सूर्य → उत्पादक → शाकाहारी → मांसाहारी; हर स्तर पर केवल 10%।"},{"mk":3,"q":"Explain ecological pyramids.","a":["Graphical representation of trophic levels; producers at the base.","Pyramid of numbers: usually upright (grassland); inverted in a tree ecosystem.","Pyramid of biomass: upright on land; inverted in the sea (phytoplankton < fish).","Pyramid of energy: always upright."],"kn":"ಸಂಖ್ಯೆ, ಜೈವದ್ರವ್ಯ, ಶಕ್ತಿ ಪಿರಮಿಡ್; ಶಕ್ತಿ ಪಿರಮಿಡ್ ಯಾವಾಗಲೂ ನೇರ.","hi":"संख्या, जैवभार, ऊर्जा पिरामिड; ऊर्जा पिरामिड सदा सीधा।"},{"mk":3,"q":"Differentiate GPP and NPP.","a":["Gross primary productivity (GPP): rate of production of organic matter during photosynthesis.","Net primary productivity (NPP): biomass available to consumers.","NPP = GPP − R (R = respiration losses)."],"kn":"NPP = GPP − ಉಸಿರಾಟ ನಷ್ಟ.","hi":"NPP = GPP − श्वसन हानि।"},{"mk":2,"q":"What are standing crop and standing state?","a":["Standing crop: amount of living material (biomass) present in each trophic level at a particular time.","Standing state: amount of nutrients (C, N, P, Ca) present in the soil at a given time."],"kn":"ಸ್ಟ್ಯಾಂಡಿಂಗ್ ಕ್ರಾಪ್ = ಜೀವದ್ರವ್ಯ; ಸ್ಟ್ಯಾಂಡಿಂಗ್ ಸ್ಟೇಟ್ = ಮಣ್ಣಿನ ಪೋಷಕಾಂಶ.","hi":"खड़ी फसल = जैवभार; स्थिर अवस्था = मिट्टी के पोषक तत्व।"},{"mk":2,"q":"What factors affect the rate of decomposition?","a":["Fast when detritus is rich in nitrogen and water-soluble sugars; slow when rich in lignin and chitin.","Warm and moist conditions favour decomposition; low temperature and anaerobic conditions slow it down."],"kn":"ಬಿಸಿ, ತೇವ ವಾತಾವರಣ ವೇಗ; ಲಿಗ್ನಿನ್, ಕೈಟಿನ್ ನಿಧಾನ.","hi":"गर्म, नम वातावरण तेज़; लिग्निन, काइटिन धीमा।"}],"dia":[{"n":"Pyramid of energy","l":["Producers (base, 1000 J)","Primary consumers (100 J)","Secondary consumers (10 J)","Tertiary consumers (1 J)"]},{"n":"Pyramid of biomass in sea (inverted)","l":["Phytoplankton (small base)","Zooplankton / fish (larger)"]}],"facts":["Pyramid of energy is always upright.","Pyramid of biomass in the sea is inverted.","10% law was given by Lindeman.","PAR is less than 50% of incident solar radiation.","Earthworm is a detritivore (farmer's friend).","NPP = GPP − respiration.","Annual NPP of the biosphere is about 170 billion tons (dry weight).","Food chain always starts with a producer (or detritus)."],"trick":["Decomposition \"F-L-C-H-M\" = Fragmentation, Leaching, Catabolism, Humification, Mineralisation (\"Five Little Cats Hate Mice\").","Energy pyramid = \"Ever upright\"."],"bp":[1,0,1,0]},{"ch":13,"t":"Biodiversity and Conservation","m":"4","plan":"Learn in-situ vs ex-situ conservation, the causes of biodiversity loss (\"Evil Quartet\") and the species–area graph. Numbers and named examples score 1-markers.","kn":"ಜೀವವೈವಿಧ್ಯ ಎಂದರೇನು, ಅದು ಏಕೆ ನಾಶವಾಗುತ್ತಿದೆ ಮತ್ತು ಅದನ್ನು ಹೇಗೆ ಸಂರಕ್ಷಿಸಬೇಕು (ಸ್ಥಳದಲ್ಲೇ / ಸ್ಥಳದ ಹೊರಗೆ).","hi":"जैव विविधता क्या है, यह क्यों घट रही है और इसका संरक्षण कैसे करें (स्वस्थाने / बाह्यस्थाने)।","qs":[{"mk":5,"q":"Explain in-situ and ex-situ conservation.","a":["In-situ (on-site): protecting organisms in their natural habitat.","Examples: biodiversity hotspots, national parks, wildlife sanctuaries, biosphere reserves, sacred groves.","India has 14 biosphere reserves, 90 national parks and 448 wildlife sanctuaries (NCERT figures).","Ex-situ (off-site): protecting threatened species outside their natural habitat.","Examples: zoological parks, botanical gardens, wildlife safari parks, seed banks.","Cryopreservation of gametes, in vitro fertilisation and tissue culture also help."],"kn":"ಸ್ಥಳದಲ್ಲೇ: ರಾಷ್ಟ್ರೀಯ ಉದ್ಯಾನ, ಅಭಯಾರಣ್ಯ; ಹೊರಗೆ: ಮೃಗಾಲಯ, ಬೀಜ ಬ್ಯಾಂಕ್.","hi":"स्वस्थाने: राष्ट्रीय उद्यान, अभयारण्य; बाह्यस्थाने: चिड़ियाघर, बीज बैंक।"},{"mk":5,"q":"What are the causes of biodiversity loss (the Evil Quartet)?","a":["Habitat loss and fragmentation — most important cause (e.g. Amazon rainforest cleared for soybean and cattle).","Over-exploitation — Steller's sea cow and passenger pigeon became extinct.","Alien species invasion — Nile perch in Lake Victoria killed cichlid fish; Parthenium, Lantana, water hyacinth; African catfish (Clarias gariepinus).","Co-extinctions — when a host fish dies, its specific parasites also die."],"kn":"ವಾಸಸ್ಥಾನ ನಾಶ, ಅತಿಯಾದ ಬಳಕೆ, ಪರಕೀಯ ಪ್ರಭೇದ, ಸಹ-ಅಳಿವು.","hi":"आवास क्षति, अति दोहन, विदेशी जातियाँ, सह-विलुप्ति।"},{"mk":3,"q":"Explain the species–area relationship.","a":["Given by Alexander von Humboldt.","Within a region, species richness increases with explored area, but only up to a limit.","Relation is a rectangular hyperbola; on a log scale it is a straight line: log S = log C + Z log A.","Z (slope) is 0.1–0.2 for small areas; 0.6–1.2 for very large areas like whole continents."],"kn":"ಪ್ರದೇಶ ಹೆಚ್ಚಾದಂತೆ ಪ್ರಭೇದ ಸಂಖ್ಯೆ ಹೆಚ್ಚು; log S = log C + Z log A.","hi":"क्षेत्र बढ़ने पर जाति संख्या बढ़ती है; log S = log C + Z log A।"},{"mk":3,"q":"Why is biodiversity higher in the tropics?","a":["Tropics remained undisturbed for millions of years — more time for species diversification.","Less seasonal, more constant and predictable environment → niche specialisation.","More solar energy → higher productivity."],"kn":"ಹೆಚ್ಚು ಕಾಲ ಅಡಚಣೆ ಇಲ್ಲ, ಸ್ಥಿರ ಹವಾಮಾನ, ಹೆಚ್ಚು ಸೂರ್ಯಶಕ್ತಿ.","hi":"लंबे समय तक अबाधित, स्थिर जलवायु, अधिक सौर ऊर्जा।"},{"mk":3,"q":"Write the three levels of biodiversity.","a":["Genetic diversity: variation within a species (e.g. 50,000 strains of rice, 1000 varieties of mango in India).","Species diversity: variety of species in a region (Western Ghats has more amphibian species than Eastern Ghats).","Ecological diversity: variety of ecosystems (India: deserts, rain forests, mangroves, coral reefs, alpine meadows)."],"kn":"ಆನುವಂಶಿಕ, ಪ್ರಭೇದ, ಪರಿಸರ ವೈವಿಧ್ಯ.","hi":"आनुवंशिक, जातीय, पारिस्थितिक विविधता।"},{"mk":2,"q":"What are biodiversity hotspots? How many are there?","a":["Regions with very high species richness and high endemism that are under threat.","There are 34 hotspots in the world; India has Western Ghats–Sri Lanka, Indo-Burma and Himalaya."],"kn":"ಹೆಚ್ಚು ಪ್ರಭೇದ + ಸ್ಥಳೀಯತೆ; ಜಗತ್ತಿನಲ್ಲಿ 34.","hi":"अधिक जातियाँ + स्थानिकता; दुनिया में 34।"},{"mk":2,"q":"What are sacred groves? Give examples.","a":["Forest patches protected by tribal communities for religious reasons.","Khasi and Jaintia hills (Meghalaya), Aravalli hills (Rajasthan), Western Ghats (Karnataka, Maharashtra), Sarguja, Chanda, Bastar (Madhya Pradesh)."],"kn":"ಧಾರ್ಮಿಕ ಕಾರಣಕ್ಕೆ ರಕ್ಷಿಸಿದ ಕಾಡು — ದೇವರ ಕಾಡು.","hi":"धार्मिक कारणों से संरक्षित वन — पवित्र उपवन।"}],"dia":[{"n":"Species–area relationship graph","l":["Area on X-axis","Species richness on Y-axis","Rectangular hyperbola","Inset: log S vs log A — straight line, slope Z"]}],"facts":["Term biodiversity was popularised by Edward Wilson.","India has about 2.4% of the world's land area but 8.1% of global species diversity.","There are 34 biodiversity hotspots in the world.","Earth Summit: Rio de Janeiro, 1992; World Summit on Sustainable Development: Johannesburg, 2002.","Steller's sea cow and passenger pigeon became extinct by over-exploitation.","Nile perch in Lake Victoria wiped out cichlid fish.","Habitat loss is the main cause of biodiversity loss.","The Amazon rainforest is called the \"lungs of the planet\"."],"trick":["Evil Quartet \"H-O-A-C\" = Habitat loss, Over-exploitation, Alien species, Co-extinction (\"HOw Are Cats\").","In-situ = \"In its own home\"; Ex-situ = \"Exit from home\"."],"bp":[2,1,0,0]}];
